                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3913dab3-ceaf-3d6c-a7de-baf480d71636",
                        "entry_id": "b89c6ab7-581c-3182-b08f-2a3b014395f2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "физ. нестабильная элементарная частица, относящаяся к заряженным лептонам и имеющая массу около 106 МэВ"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c2d41680-239f-4099-a83f-649d8c8d622c",
                                "sense_id": "3913dab3-ceaf-3d6c-a7de-baf480d71636",
                                "text": "Положительный мюон."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c48ae42b-31bf-4461-bfc7-85f2cf9edf09",
                                "sense_id": "3913dab3-ceaf-3d6c-a7de-baf480d71636",
                                "text": "Отрицательный мюон в большинстве случаев распадается на электрон, электронное антинейтрино и мюонное нейтрино."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "41915ae4-bb3d-37dc-86ac-b016324b9774",
                        "entry_id": "b89c6ab7-581c-3182-b08f-2a3b014395f2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "физ. мюон [1] с отрицательным электрическим зарядом и спином ½"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fd7db8d2-cbeb-4bf1-ad9f-c5d9469f8e62",
                                "sense_id": "41915ae4-bb3d-37dc-86ac-b016324b9774",
                                "text": "Мюон, в отличие от антимюона, отрицательно заряжен и может замещать электрон в атомных оболочках."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "580cb810-01b4-40a4-8a38-0e2810006fb6",
                        "source_entry_id": "b89c6ab7-581c-3182-b08f-2a3b014395f2",
                        "source_sense_description": "в обоих смыслах?",
                        "target_lang_word": "muon",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "muon",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6db1e4b9-4f7a-304a-9d35-a2720167fe53",
                                        "entry_id": "28b3bd39-b592-366d-ba4d-ff5872407aea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An unstable elementary particle in the lepton family, having similar properties to the electron but with a mass 207 times greater."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d3640b4f-53a1-4b79-b6b7-35246d3b0182",
                                                "sense_id": "6db1e4b9-4f7a-304a-9d35-a2720167fe53",
                                                "text": "The μ-meson of Powell (called here muon) is instead a disintegration product of the pion, only weakly linked to the nucleons and therefore of little importance in the explanation of nuclear forces."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ad6ab89e-7010-4dfa-9ae4-0fc68c4f7137",
                                                "sense_id": "6db1e4b9-4f7a-304a-9d35-a2720167fe53",
                                                "text": "The spectrum of electrons arising from the decay of the negative mu meson has been determined. The muons are arrested in the gas of a high pressure hydrogen filled diffusion cloud chamber."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0bee3996-50e4-4fe6-a1cc-b40ffa89b0bd",
                                                "sense_id": "6db1e4b9-4f7a-304a-9d35-a2720167fe53",
                                                "text": "The data comes from experiments at the Fermilab US particle accelerator facility, which explored how subatomic particles called muons – similar to electrons but about 200 times heavier – move in a magnetic field."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "34cfafa8-8e5d-46a2-868f-e5f0f1385afe",
                        "source_entry_id": "b89c6ab7-581c-3182-b08f-2a3b014395f2",
